  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, establishing RNA as the stronger modality, while config_010 (image_only, resnet50) is very weak at 20.8%. The key uncertainty is whether moving from a single profile to multiple profiles with aggregation improves the RNA representation. config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the minimal extension of config_001—it changes only the profile setting and adds avgpool aggregation while keeping the same PCA encoder. This cleanly isolates the effect of multiprofile aggregation. It is the best use of the next budget slot because: (1) it directly builds on our best-performing configuration with a single structural change, (2) the result informs whether multiprofile+aggregation is worth pursuing across all RNA encoders and in multimodal settings, and (3) if it fails to improve over config_001, we can deprioritize the entire multiprofile branch and focus on encoder choice or image improvements instead."
}

